# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# One rule per URL that was once live and is not any more. These are permanent
# (301) because the content genuinely moved, which is what tells Google to
# transfer the old page's ranking to the new one rather than treat it as a
# soft 404 and drop it.
#
# Never delete a line from this file. A redirect costs nothing to keep and the
# links pointing at these URLs — search results, bookmarks, other people's
# posts — do not expire.

# Merged into the converter, which now shows the live epoch as well. The two
# pages were competing for the same search intent and people almost always
# wanted both at once.
/tools/current-unix-timestamp  /tools/unix-timestamp-converter  301
